  data:  # 2d74
    kind: invariant  # 2d74
    title: "smart-test leaves out a test that reaches a changed module through another module's import: a changed constant breaks a test PR CI never runs"  # 2d74
    status: violated  # 2d74
    priority: 2  # 2d74
    parent:  # 2d74
    tags:  # 2d74
    - smart_test  # 2d74
    - ci_infrastructure  # 2d74
    - test_selection  # 2d74
    isbefore: []  # 2d74
    duplicate_of: []  # 2d74
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 2d74
    pr_ref:  # 2d74
    description: "Found 2026-11-14 while running the WI-falas soundness check on the smart-test bed. Evidence: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/falas_measure_11142026/slice_gap and bed_results.txt.\n\nOBSERVED ON THE REAL REPO (dev b373512b77). One constant changed in packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/schema.py: STABLE_ID_SCHEME = \"hypergumbo-stableid-v14\" became \"hg-stableid-v14\".\n- scripts/smart-test --manifest: exit 0, mode targeted, slice \"Found 236 dependent files\", narrowing refused (import-time change), 252 test files selected. packages/hypergumbo-core/tests/test_stable_shape_ids.py is not among them (grep -c gives 0; the manifest is kept as slice_gap/real_manifest_for_schema_constant.txt).\n- scripts/smart-test packages/hypergumbo-core/tests/test_stable_shape_ids.py on that tree: exit 1, \"1 failed, 14 passed\", FAILED test_output_includes_scheme_identifiers (it asserts data[\"stable_id_scheme\"].startswith(\"hypergumbo-stableid-\")).\nSo a PR making that change passes PR CI with a failing test on dev. The twice-daily full suite is the first run that would show it.\n\nHOW MANY TESTS ARE IN THAT POSITION FOR THIS ONE FILE. The slice of schema.py lists 236 files: 209 test files and 10 source files, 3 of which import schema at top level. 93 test files outside the slice import one of those 3 modules at top level (all 93 through hypergumbo_core.cli); none of the 93 imports schema itself. List: slice_gap/schema_candidates.txt, script slice_gap/candidates.py. Importing cli runs schema's import-time code, so each of the 93 is reached by an import-time change of schema.py. How many of the 93 would change outcome for a given edit was not measured; one was shown to (above).\n\nTHE MECHANISM, ISOLATED ON THE BED (a scratch copy with four added modules). For a change to consts.py the slice lists every module that imports consts, and then:\n- a test of a module whose FUNCTION CALLS a consts function: selected;\n- a test of a module that reads consts.LIMIT_A as an attribute of the module object: not selected;\n- a test of a module that does from consts import LIMIT_A and reads the name in a function: not selected;\n- a test of a module that calls a consts function AT IMPORT and keeps the result in a global: not selected.\nUnder the bed's mutation oracle (raise at the top of the changed block) each of the three unselected tests fails, so each is MUST-select. On the bed's falas-unsafe-* edits and on falas-enumerated-public the static selection, the manifest and the narrowed set all leave out such a test (bed_results.txt, the rows whose DROPPED MUST names a file that narrowing did not drop: user, surface).\n\nWHY. hypergumbo slice --files is a reverse slice from the symbols of the changed files. A module that imports the changed file is listed through its file-level import edge. A test that imports a function of that module is reached only when a chain of call edges leads from that function to a symbol of the changed file. Reading a constant, reading an attribute of the module object, or using a value computed at import is not a call edge. The unions smart-test adds do not close it: the coverage union selects by rows on changed blocks, and a module-level statement runs under no test's context, so it has no rows; the read record covers reads of the file as data.\n\nSIZE OF THE EXPOSED CHANGE CLASS. Over the 90 PRs that changed package source between 10-30 and 11-14, 28 changed the value of a computed module-level assignment, 10 changed the value of a literal constant, 12 added a computed assignment (falas_measure_11142026/report_prs150.txt). Those are the changes for which a module that only reads the value is a dependent.\n\nNOT VERIFIED. Whether the stable hypergumbo that smart-test uses (9.0.0, pipx) and dev's slicer differ here; the bed and the real run both used the stable build, which is what smart-test runs. Whether the Python analyzer emits a reference edge for an imported constant that the slicer could follow. How many real PRs merged with a test broken this way (it would show as a red full-suite cron after a green PR).\n\nDIRECTIONS, NOT A PRESCRIPTION. (a) Make the selection import-transitive at file level for import-time changes: when a changed block is import-time, every test file whose import closure contains the file is selected (the closure exists in the same graph). Cost: larger selections for hub modules; measure before choosing. (b) Give the slicer an edge for name and attribute reads of module-level symbols. (c) Record which modules each test file loads (sys.modules at teardown) in the selection index and select by that record for import-time changes.\n\nGENERALITY. Any package source file, any module-level state another module reads; not keyed to schema.py.\n\nDONE WHEN. The filed real-repo change (the STABLE_ID_SCHEME edit) selects test_stable_shape_ids.py; the bed carries the three unselected shapes as scenarios and scores no dropped MUST for them; the selection-size cost on the last 90 source-changing PRs is reported."  # 2d74
    fields:  # 2d74
      statement: "When import-time code of a package source file changes, every test file that imports that file, directly or through other package modules, is in the selection PR CI runs."  # 2d74
      root_cause: "hypergumbo slice --files is a reverse slice from the symbols of the changed file: a module importing the file is listed, but a test of that module is reached only through a chain of call edges into the changed file, and a constant read, a module attribute read or a value computed at import is not a call edge. The coverage union cannot add it because module-level statements have no coverage rows."  # 2d74
- op: discuss  # bca7
  at: '2026-11-14T22:01:32Z'  # bca7
  by: agent  # bca7
  actor: jgstern_agent  # bca7
  clock: 2  # bca7
  nonce: bca7  # bca7
  message: "OWNER RULING 2026-11-14: fix it by import closure, counting module-level AND function-level (lazy) imports. Cost measured before the ruling over the 90 source-changing PRs of 10-30 to 11-14 (evidence: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/mikag_cost_11142026): the closure is taken for each changed source file whose import-time code changed; module-level imports only add 5 percent test seconds (38 PRs grow, median share of the suite 52 to 56 percent); with lazy imports 18 percent (47 PRs grow, median 68 percent). Both select test_stable_shape_ids.py for the schema.py constant. Not in the ruling and measured afterwards: taking the closure for ANY code change instead of import-time changes only would cost 28 percent (median share 88 percent), so the trigger stays the import-time change."  # bca7
