- op: discuss  # 35ec
  at: '2026-11-15T00:38:07Z'  # 35ec
  by: agent  # 35ec
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 35ec
  clock: 4  # 35ec
  nonce: 35ec  # 35ec
  message: "FIXED in PR #2186 (dev 2b669a5414). WHAT SHIPPED: hypergumbo_core/import_closure.py builds a file-level import graph of the tree (every import statement anywhere in a file, module-level and inside functions per the owner ruling of 2026-11-14, except under if TYPE_CHECKING; parent packages; literal import_module; for a test the conftest.py files above it and sibling helpers); coverage-select import-closure names the test files whose imports reach a source file whose module or class body changed, or that was deleted; smart-test adds them to the manifest above the seam (--no-import-union turns it off). FILED REPRO RE-RUN on merged dev 2b669a5414 (evidence: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/mikag_cost_11142026/after_merge): STABLE_ID_SCHEME in schema.py changed to hg-stableid-v14, scripts/smart-test --manifest exits 0, mode targeted, and the manifest holds packages/hypergumbo-core/tests/test_stable_shape_ids.py (grep -c gives 1; before the fix 0). The manifest header reads Import-closure tests: 1162 added, 1414 selected (before the fix 252). On that tree scripts/smart-test packages/hypergumbo-core/tests/test_stable_shape_ids.py exits 1, 1 failed 14 passed, FAILED test_output_includes_scheme_identifiers: the test that fails is now in the selection PR CI runs. Both files restored. BED: edit constant-read-elsewhere scores no dropped MUST in manifest, union and narrow (the four readers: module attribute, imported name, value computed at import, lazy import); delete-module-and-edit selects the test still importing a deleted module; tests/test_smart_test_bed.py pins both, with 9.0.0 and with 9.2.0 slicing. COST OF THE SHIPPED RULE, replayed with the merged module over the 90 PRs that changed package source between 10-30 and 11-14 (after_merge/real_cost_out.txt): 48 PRs grow, selected test seconds 232518 to 291318, PLUS 25.3 PERCENT, median share of the suite 52 to 68 percent. THIS IS HIGHER THAN THE 18 PERCENT I REPORTED BEFORE THE RULING. Cause (after_merge/variants_out.txt): the root conftest.py imports hypergumbo_core.analyze.registry inside a fixture; the shipped graph counts the package above an imported module, so every test file reaches hypergumbo_core/__init__.py, which imports ir at module level, and ir reaches catalog and catalog reaches cli through imports inside functions. So a file anywhere in the import closure of cli is loaded by all 1414 test files, and an import-time change to one selects the whole suite as a targeted run. The pre-build estimate had the conftest edge without the package above it. Same replay under other graphs: conftest chain not counted 17.8 percent; imports inside functions counted only in test files and conftest.py 9.8 percent (median share 56); module-level only 5.3 percent; each still selects test_stable_shape_ids.py for the filed change. The merged docs (ADR-0010, the module docstring) carry the 18 percent figure labelled as measured before the build; correcting them rides with the next PR. Which graph to keep is the owner's decision. NOT ASSERTED: an import whose name is computed at runtime (entry points, registries of dotted strings) is not an edge, and no test of that shape was run. RESIDUAL filed separately: a changed FUNCTION body that another module calls at import (bed edit body-edit-limits still drops test_reads_at_import.py)."  # 35ec
